💡 **SUGGESTION: identical `if (Platform.isMacOS)` branches — the conditional still asserts nothing (second posting; thread PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6vCk5L)**

Unchanged in this round — both arms of the self-update zip-fallback test execute byte-identical statements; only the comments differ:

```dart
if (Platform.isMacOS) {
  // The archive miss routes into _zipAssetName's stable zip; ...
  expect(code, 1);
  expect(target.readAsStringSync(), 'old');
} else {
  // No zip fallback off macOS: the download failure stands.
  expect(code, 1);
  expect(target.readAsStringSync(), 'old');
}
```

Either drop the conditional, or make the macOS arm actually distinguish the fallback: assert the `MockClient` received the request for the `_macZipAssets` asset name on macOS (and none on other platforms) before the provenance abort. As-is the `if` suggests platform-divergent coverage the assertions don't deliver.

